# Shell scripts run on the Pi, which is Linux. If this repo is cloned on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true, git rewrites them with CRLF line endings and
# the shebang line becomes "#!/bin/bash\r" -- the kernel then looks for an
# interpreter literally named "bash\r" and reports "bad interpreter: No such
# file or directory", which points at bash rather than at the line endings.
#
# run_camera_service.sh is the one that matters: it is the only supported way
# to launch the camera service, because it exports LIBCAMERA_RPI_TUNING_FILE
# before libcamera can resolve the tuning path.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything the Pi executes directly.
*.py text eol=lf

# Line-ending normalisation would corrupt these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pt binary
